# Written by the build-kernel CI job (os/kernel/Containerfile). The
# digest-pinned tilo-kernel repo the OS image installs from — swapping
# Fedora's kernel-core → tilo-kernel-core.  Bump by re-running the
# build-kernel workflow; it prints the new KERNEL_RPMS_REF at the end.
#
# INITIAL SEED: the tag below is the mutable :latest tag; before the first
# CI publish this file is deliberately unpinned (no digest yet).  The
# build-image workflow's step "Load KERNEL_RPMS_REF" reads whatever is
# here — if the first build-kernel run hasn't happened, the OS build fails
# fast with "manifest unknown" on the FROM.  That's intentional (no
# silent fall-through to Fedora's stock kernel).
KERNEL_RPMS_REF=code.podesta.ai/qos/qos-kernel@sha256:f932be5b8c0df334b853c3436e7b912885c28133cb9ff7aea79adf83e7f822fd
